  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 405 AM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nEnsemble guidance continues to show chances of rain Wednesday \nnight and into Thursday due to forcing driven by upper-level \ndivergence, low-level warm air advection, and a shortwave over \nnorthern IL and southern WI, although estimated rainfall totals \nare trending down. Current guidance is indicating rainfall \ntotals of 0.1 to 0.5 inches in the northern part of our forecast\nregion, while the southern part of the forecast region may only\nsee closer to 0.1. As a result, dangerous heat and humidity \nwill continue to impact the region on Wednesday.\n\nThe latest guidance is continuing to agree that an upper level\nridge will remain over the Mid-Mississippi Valley Thursday\nthrough the weekend. As a result, the cold front that was\nexpected to move into the region may not make it as far south as\ninitially expected, stalling in far northern MO and southern IA.\nNortheastern MO and west-central IL could see some minor relief,\ndropping temperatures several degrees compared to the rest of\nour forecast area. Despite the potential relief, potentially\nimpactful heat may return this weekend by the weekend, but\nconfidence is low with temperature IQRs of 10-15 degrees\nThursday through Sunday due to the uncertainty in how far south\nthe cold front progresses. Meanwhile the guidance is indicating\nthat the temperatures for the rest of our region could be\ncomparable with the temperatures we have seen over the last\ncouple of days. The rainfall forecast for the region has also\nbeen impacted due to the cold front forecasted to remain farther\nnorth than previously forecasted, with cluster analysis\nproviding higher confidence that the swath of heavy rain\nremaining more north in southern IA.",
